# Conventional Commit header: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#   Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore, build, ci
#   Example: feat(bluetooth): add RFCOMM transport support
#
# What / Why / Testing Notes: a few bullets each, prose within each
# bullet. Group related changes into one bullet rather than listing
# every file/detail separately -- aim for 2-3 bullets per section, not
# an exhaustive itemized list.
#
# No Co-Authored-By trailer on commits in this repo.
#
# Lines starting with '#' are stripped automatically.
